UI conventions
==============

Colours come from the token palette only - src/constants/palette.js.
Do not use Tailwind's default colour families (blue-*, indigo-*, slate-*,
green-*, red-*, yellow-*). Use the semantic names instead:

  primary-*   accent / interactive        (primary-600 = #2563EB)
  gray-*      all neutrals (slate scale)  (page bg = gray-50, borders = gray-200)
  success-*   correct answers, verified
  danger-*    incorrect answers, destructive actions
  warning-*   caution, upcoming features

Primary button      : bg-primary-600 text-white hover:bg-primary-700
Secondary button    : bg-white text-gray-700 border border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50
Card / panel        : bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl
Page background     : bg-gray-50
Header / footer     : bg-white with a border-gray-200 hairline
Control height      : h-9 (compact) or h-10 (default)
Page gutter         : layout.container from src/constants/designTokens.js
                      (max-w-[1800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8)
                      The header and every page body must use it so the left/right
                      edges line up. Do not hand-roll a container.
Advertising         : left/right rails only (components/common/AdRail), never in
                      the content column. Rails are xl+ only.

NOTE on tailwind.config.js: all custom scales must go inside `theme.extend`.
Declaring maxWidth/minWidth/zIndex at the `theme` root replaces Tailwind's
defaults and silently kills standard classes like max-w-7xl, min-w-0 and z-50.

Prefer the shared primitives in src/components/common (Button, Card, Badge,
EmptyState, PageContainer, MathContent) over re-styling from scratch.

Rich text from the API (question bodies, options, solutions, comments) must be
rendered through MathContent / JSXUtils.htmlDecode so it is sanitised and its
$$...$$ LaTeX is typeset.
